<mjml lang="en">
  <mj-head>
    <!--
      PROBE — .flush-mobile, the two-rule gutter fix (2026-08-13).
      Not a catalog page. Send dist/probe_flush-mobile_live.html through EN to
      EoA and read android16_gmailapp_pixel10_* and iphone17_* first, then
      confirm DESKTOP is untouched in gmailcom-* and applemail16.

      WHAT IS ALREADY PROVEN (probe pTdFUx7a, measured not eyeballed)
      There is no column-shrink bug: the image always fills its column, and
      the narrow look is gutter on a ~333 CSS px screen. Measured image
      widths there: control 262.7 CSS, flush-authored 332.7 (= the container
      exactly), and — the key result — a CONTROL-markup card carrying only a
      class-only mobile rule reached 326.3. So `.class td` DOES reach Gmail,
      where child combinators (EN escapes them) and attribute selectors
      (inert in Gmail) both fail. Mobile gutters are fixable in CSS with
      desktop untouched.

      WHAT THAT PROBE ALSO EXPOSED
      The blunt rule strips the body copy's inset too, and it makes caption
      alignment WORSE. Caption offset from the photo's left edge, same run:
      control +49.7 CSS, blunt-rule +46.7, flush-authored +56.7. The photo
      goes edge-to-edge while the caption stays put, so it ends up stranded
      between the photo edge and the text column. This reproduces the QA
      report's "captions appear off the edge of the image".

      THE PROPOSAL UNDER TEST
      Two rules. The first takes every gutter to zero on mobile; the second
      puts a deliberate inset back on text only. `.wysiwyg` and `.caption`
      sit on their own <td>s (verified in the compiled output), and a
      two-class selector outranks `.flush-mobile td`, so the second rule wins
      where it applies.

      VARIANTS (identical markup; only the CSS class on the section differs)

        H1 CONTROL   no class. The baseline to measure against.
        H2 INSET     .flush-mobile. Images flush to the screen edge; text AND
                     caption inset 16px. Caption aligns with the body column.
        H3 CAP-FLUSH .flush-mobile-capflush. Same, except the caption keeps
                     zero inset so it aligns with the PHOTO's left edge
                     instead of the text.

      H2 vs H3 is a taste call and the reason both are here: with the photo
      full-bleed the caption cannot align with both the photo and the copy.
      Pick from the render.

      WHAT RUN 1 ALREADY SETTLED (test exYrw8U6, measured)
      Images: H1 262.7 CSS, H2 332.7, H3 326.0. Body copy held its inset at
      29 CSS in BOTH H2 and H3, so the two-class override beats
      `.flush-mobile td` in Gmail. Desktop rendered identical to the control
      in Apple Mail. The mechanism works; both caption treatments are viable.

      WHAT THIS RUN ADDS — the incumbent .caption rule
      Run 1 omitted the catalog's own `.caption { padding-left: 16px }`, so
      the new rules were never tested against the rule they will actually sit
      beside. Predicted resolution, by specificity:

        H2  `.flush-mobile .caption` (0,2,0) beats both the incumbent
            `.caption` (0,1,0) and `.flush-mobile td` (0,1,1)  -> 16px inset
        H3  `.flush-mobile-capflush td` (0,1,1) beats the incumbent
            `.caption` (0,1,0)                                 -> 0, flush

      If H3's caption comes back INSET rather than flush, the incumbent won
      and it has to be removed from the catalog rather than left to fight.

      VERDICT RULE
      1. H2/H3 images stay ~326-333 CSS px, H1 stays ~262 (regression check).
      2. H2/H3 body copy keeps its inset (regression check).
      3. H2 caption inset, H3 caption FLUSH with the photo — the new result.
      4. DESKTOP identical across all three (regression check).
    -->
    <mj-breakpoint width="600px" />
    <mj-title>PROBE — flush-mobile</mj-title>

    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-text
        color="#000000"
        font-size="18px"
        font-weight="400"
        font-family="Tahoma, sans-serif"
        line-height="24px"
        css-class="wysiwyg"
      />
      <mj-image padding="0" />
    </mj-attributes>

    <mj-style>
      @media (max-width: 599px) {
        /* THE INCUMBENT. Copied verbatim from tpl_unified-blocks.mjml so the
           new rules are tested against what they will actually coexist with.
           The first run of this probe omitted it, which left the interaction
           below unproven. */
        .caption {
          padding-left: 16px !important;
          padding-right: 16px !important;
        }

        /* No child combinator (EN escapes those) and no attribute selector
           (inert in Gmail). Class-only descendant is the one form proven to
           reach every client — probe pTdFUx7a, 2026-08-13. */
        .flush-mobile td,
        .flush-mobile-capflush td {
          padding-left: 0 !important;
          padding-right: 0 !important;
        }

        /* Two classes outrank `.flush-mobile td`, so the inset comes back
           for copy only. Images keep the flush treatment above. */
        .flush-mobile .wysiwyg,
        .flush-mobile .caption,
        .flush-mobile-capflush .wysiwyg {
          padding-left: 16px !important;
          padding-right: 16px !important;
        }
      }
    </mj-style>

    <mj-raw>
      <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="format-detection" content="telephone=no" />
    </mj-raw>
    <mj-include path="./styles.css" type="css" />
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body css-class="email-body" background-color="#ffffff">

    <!-- START: Flush Label H1 -->
    <mj-section css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">H1 — CONTROL (NO CLASS)</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Flush Label H1 -->

    <!-- START: Flush H1 Control -->
    <mj-section css-class="two-col-image-text-block block" background-color="#ffffff" padding="16px 32px">
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column first-column" width="240px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-image src="assets/photo-garden.jpg" width="224px" alt="Children exploring plants in a schoolyard garden" padding="0" align="center" fluid-on-mobile="true" css-class="two-col-image" />
        <mj-text css-class="caption" align="left" font-size="10px" line-height="16px" padding="8px 0 0 0">Caption — watch where this sits.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column" width="296px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-text padding="0 0 8px"><h3 style="margin:0;">H1 control heading.</h3></mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0">Body copy — this should keep a readable inset in H2 and H3, never run to the screen edge.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Flush H1 Control -->

    <!-- START: Flush Label H2 -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">H2 — FLUSH, CAPTION WITH THE COPY</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Flush Label H2 -->

    <!-- START: Flush H2 Inset -->
    <mj-section css-class="two-col-image-text-block block flush-mobile" background-color="#ffffff" padding="16px 32px">
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column first-column" width="240px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-image src="assets/photo-garden.jpg" width="224px" alt="Children exploring plants in a schoolyard garden" padding="0" align="center" fluid-on-mobile="true" css-class="two-col-image" />
        <mj-text css-class="caption" align="left" font-size="10px" line-height="16px" padding="8px 0 0 0">Caption — should align with the BODY COPY.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column" width="296px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-text padding="0 0 8px"><h3 style="margin:0;">H2 inset heading.</h3></mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0">Body copy — this should keep a readable inset in H2 and H3, never run to the screen edge.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Flush H2 Inset -->

    <!-- START: Flush Label H3 -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">H3 — FLUSH, CAPTION WITH THE PHOTO</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Flush Label H3 -->

    <!-- START: Flush H3 Capflush -->
    <mj-section css-class="two-col-image-text-block block flush-mobile-capflush" background-color="#ffffff" padding="16px 32px">
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column first-column" width="240px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-image src="assets/photo-garden.jpg" width="224px" alt="Children exploring plants in a schoolyard garden" padding="0" align="center" fluid-on-mobile="true" css-class="two-col-image" />
        <mj-text css-class="caption" align="left" font-size="10px" line-height="16px" padding="8px 0 0 0">Caption — should align with the PHOTO's left edge.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
      <mj-column css-class="two-col-column" width="296px" vertical-align="top" padding="0 8px">
        <mj-text padding="0 0 8px"><h3 style="margin:0;">H3 cap-flush heading.</h3></mj-text>
        <mj-text padding="0">Body copy — this should keep a readable inset in H2 and H3, never run to the screen edge.</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Flush H3 Capflush -->

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
